<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The assassination of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a>, heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne, took place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a> in 1914. He and his wife were shot by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a>, a Bosnian Serb nationalist. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>'s response led to the outbreak of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, which ended with the dissolution of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assassination-of-archduke-franz-ferdinand.jpg" alt="Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Achille Beltrame · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DC-1914-27-d-Sarajevo-cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
